    <tok fileIndex="0" linenr="1851" column="3" str="/* In UDP, there is a maximum theoretical packet paload length andx   * a minimum payload length that is &quot;guaranteed&quot; to work.x   * To detect if this minimum payload can be increased, ngtcp2 sendsx   * now and then a packet payload larger than the minimum. It thatx   * is ACKed by the peer, both parties know that it works andx   * the subsequent packets can use a larger one.x   * This is called PMTUD (Path Maximum Transmission Unit Discovery).x   * Since a PMTUD might be rejected right on send, we do not want itx   * be followed by other packets of lesser size. Because those wouldx   * also fail then. So, if we detect a PMTUD while buffering, we flush.x   */"/>
